---
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';

const items = [
  [
    {
      question: 'What is CachyOS?',
      answer: `CachyOS is a performance-optimized Arch Linux distribution. Every package is compiled with modern CPU instruction sets like x86-64-v3/v4 and Zen4, plus LTO and PGO optimizations. It ships a custom kernel with advanced scheduler options, giving you a noticeably faster Arch Linux experience while maintaining full rolling-release flexibility.`,
    },
    {
      question: 'How is CachyOS different from regular Arch Linux?',
      answer: `Standard Arch Linux ships generic x86-64 binaries. CachyOS rebuilds the entire stack with CPU-specific optimizations targeting x86-64-v3, x86-64-v4, and Zen4 architectures. Core packages receive additional PGO and BOLT optimization passes. The custom linux-cachyos kernel includes tuned schedulers like BORE, sched-ext, and BMQ for better responsiveness.

You also get two installer options (graphical Calamares or CLI), 17+ desktop environments, and pre-configured optimizations out of the box.`,
    },
    {
      question: 'Which desktop environments are available?',
      answer: `You can choose from over 17 desktop environments and window managers during installation, including KDE Plasma, GNOME, COSMIC, Hyprland, Sway, Niri, i3, XFCE, and more. Every option is fully supported and configured out of the box.`,
    },
  ],
  [
    {
      question: 'Is CachyOS compatible with Arch Linux AUR?',
      answer: `Yes. CachyOS is fully compatible with the Arch Linux AUR (Arch User Repository). You can use any AUR helper like yay, paru, or pamac to install packages from the AUR. All Arch Linux packages and documentation are compatible with CachyOS.`,
    },
    {
      question: 'What hardware does CachyOS support?',
      answer: `CachyOS supports x86-64 hardware with a focus on modern CPUs. We offer optimized builds for x86-64-v3 (Haswell and newer), x86-64-v4 (modern high-end CPUs), and Zen4 architectures. The Handheld Edition supports ROG Ally, Steam Deck OLED/LCD, Legion Go, and Lenovo Legion Go S.`,
    },
    {
      question: 'How can I support the project?',
      answer: `CachyOS is an independent, community-driven project. You can support us through donations via Bitcoin, Ethereum, Litecoin, or Patreon. Your contributions help cover infrastructure costs (mirrors, build servers, hosting), fund active development, and enable hardware testing across different architectures.`,
    },
  ],
];
---

<div class="px-4 py-16 mx-auto max-w-6xl lg:py-20">
  <div class="max-w-xl sm:mx-auto lg:max-w-2xl">
    <div class="max-w-xl mb-10 md:mx-auto sm:text-center lg:max-w-2xl md:mb-12">
      <h2
        class="max-w-lg mb-4 text-3xl font-bold leading-none tracking-tight sm:text-4xl md:mx-auto font-heading"
      >
        Frequently Asked Questions
      </h2>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="max-w-(--breakpoint-xl) sm:mx-auto">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-8 gap-y-8 lg:gap-x-16 md:grid-cols-2">
      {
        items.map((subitems) => (
          <div class="space-y-8">
            {subitems.map(({ question, answer }) => (
              <div>
                <p class="mb-4 text-xl font-bold">
                  <Icon
                    name="tabler:arrow-down-right"
                    class="w-7 h-7 text-primary-500 inline-block"
                  />
                  {question}
                </p>
                {answer.split('\n\n').map((paragraph) => (
                  <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-400 mb-2" set:html={paragraph} />
                ))}
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
